  "title": "Exterior & Garage Stone Ideas | February 2025 GenStone Projects",
  "description": "Explore February 2025 GenStone siding and garage upgrades. Complete home transformations that instantly boost curb appeal.",
  "canonicalUrl": "https://genstone.com/insights/project-spotlights/february-2025",
  "text": "GenStone Project Highlights – February 2025 Exterior & Garage Projects\n\nAmanda Lombard\nDirector\n\nFebruary projects focused on exterior upgrades, with homeowners improving curb appeal through targeted improvements. Garage accents and front-of-home details stood out as simple but impactful ways to elevate a home’s appearance.\nTry Visualizer Get Project Planning Guide\n\n\"Looks like real stone. Very cost-effective. Would recommend\"\n\nRobert\n\nExterior Projects\n\nExplore more exterior stone projects\n\nExterior upgrades can dramatically change the appearance of a home without requiring a full renovation. This month featured projects where homeowners added stone to facades and entry areas, creating a more finished and durable look.\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/bdh71L1Z1x6mvswBvLR7tZ.jpg\" data-uuid=\"bdh71L1Z1x6mvswBvLR7tZ\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/> 268\n\nNew Siding for Doug’s Home\nSee how Doug transformed the outside of his home using our stacked stone siding! For fireplace finish ideas, browse GenStone's home siding options today!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nStratford\n\n1\n\nDayna’s Home Siding Remodel\nDayna spent three years working on a home remodel project and used our Keystone Stacked Stone for the siding. Take a look!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKeystone\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/RQcx39aQY9GrtVsWmKJJK9.jpg\" data-uuid=\"RQcx39aQY9GrtVsWmKJJK9\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/> 1\n\nDee’s Faux Stone Window Surround\nDee used our Iron Ore faux stone to create a DIY window surround after completing a garage conversion project. Take a look!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nIron Ore\n\n2\n\nDIY Exterior Home Renovation\nLooking to give your home an update? Check out this do it yourself Exterior Home Renovation using Keystone stacked stone panels by GenStone.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nStratford\n\n32\n\nGary’s House Foundation Covering Panels\nSee how Gary George, a DIY rookie, was able to completely remodel his small back deck on his own using GenStone faux stone products. Check out his remodel here!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\n4\n\nGregory’s Faux Stone Exterior Siding\nTransform your home's exterior siding with GenStone's faux stone. You can completely remodel your home on a budget. Take a look!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/mqH9kpxw8v83vKQg28H7U9.jpg\" data-uuid=\"mqH9kpxw8v83vKQg28H7U9\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/> 2957\n\nHow Earl Covered His Old Brick Wall\nYou can cover up an old brick wall with GenStone faux stone panels. Watch how Earl, a 79 year old weekend warrior covered up his old brick.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nDesert Sunrise\n\n4\n\nJeffrey’s DIY Siding and Skirting\nYou can transform your home exterior with a stone veneer DIY siding and skirting project. Take a look at this one for inspiration!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nVanilla Bean\n\n9\n\nKaren’s Home Siding Renovation\nThis customer undertook a huge DIY home siding renovation project with GenStone. See the before and after photos of this transformation!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nCoffee\n\nKenny’s DIY Home Siding Makeover\nIf you're looking for a DIY home siding makeover project, check out Kenny's! He used GenStone's stacked stone to transform his home exterior!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\nGarage Accent Projects\n\nView more garage stone ideas\n\nGarage facades are an often-overlooked opportunity for improvement. February projects showed how stone accents can frame garage doors and add contrast, making the entire front of the home more visually appealing.\n\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/embed/v4.js\"></script><img style=\"width: 100%; margin: auto; display: block;\" class=\"vidyard-player-embed\" src=\"https://play.vidyard.com/sgv1TNWGX4NimCPJxVcatc.jpg\" data-uuid=\"sgv1TNWGX4NimCPJxVcatc\" data-v=\"4\" data-type=\"inline\" data-width=\"640\" data-height=\"360\"/> 2\n\nCarlos’ Stone Veneer DIY Garage Wainscoting\nWant to boost your curb appeal? Try a DIY garage wainscoting project using stone veneer, like Carlos did in only two days!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\n7\n\nChan’s Brick Veneer Garage Siding\nChan used our Multi Color Brick Veneer for garage siding because it matched almost perfectly with his home siding. Take a look!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nMulti Color\n\n15\n\nChris’ Brick Veneer RV Garage\nIf you need to upgrade your RV garage, our Multi Color Brick Veneer is a great siding choice. Faux brick is the perfect DIY solution!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nMulti Color\n\nAlex Padilla\nProject Coordinator\n\n57\n\nDan’s Stone Veneer Garage Front\nThis customer opted for Keystone Stacked Stone to put stone veneer around his garage front to make it stand out and be more inviting.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKeystone\n\n2\n\nDIY Faux Stone Garage Siding\nLooking for siding inspiration? Check out this DIY garage siding project that uses GenStone's Kenai faux stone for inspiration!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\n13\n\nEd’s Faux Stone DIY Garage Remodel\nThis customer did a full DIY garage remodel project using faux stone, transforming the entire garage. Check out this project!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nIron Ore\n\nAmanda Lombard\nDirector\n\n5\n\nEric’s DIY Faux Stone Garage\nFaux stone is perfect for a home DIY project — whether the project is your garage or entry, stone veneer is the solution you need!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nKenai\n\n93\n\nJohn’s Faux Stone Garage Siding and Front Door\nGenStone's faux stone offers a full siding solution, so you can enhance your garage and front door in a simple DIY project.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\n7\n\nMark’s DIY Stone Veneer Garage Wainscoting\nOur stone veneer is the perfect way to update your garage exterior, like Mike did as a DIY wainscoting project. Take a look at this project!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\n7\n\nMark’s Faux Stone Detached Garage Wainscoting\nLooking to give your garage a new look? Check out this gorgeous faux stone detached garage wainscoting using our Northern Slate!\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nNorthern Slate\n\nJagger Gottschalk\nProject Coordinator\n\n7\n\nTed’s DIY Garage Wainscoting Project\nThis GenStone customer installed our Coffee Stacked Stone panels for a small DIY wainscoting project on his garage with a big impact.\nLearn more &rarr;\n\nCoffee\n\nWhat Our Customers Are Saying\n\n“GenStone completely changed the look of the front of my house. It made a huge difference in curb appeal.”\n\n— Joel\n\n“I absolutely love the way GenStone looks on my house. I would highly recommend it.”\n\n— Lisa\n\n“The outside looks great and really improved the overall appearance of our home.”\n\n— Douglas\n\nFAQs\nAsk Away. We've Heard it All.\n\nAre GenStone panels waterproof?\n\nYes. GenStone panels are 100% waterproof when installed correctly. No flashing is required. Follow GenStone installation instructions, including using the proper amount of adhesive and caulking all connections between panels and all termination points.\n\nRob Dean\n\nSenior Project Coordinator\n\nCan GenStone be installed indoors and outdoors?\n\nYes. GenStone panels are designed for both interior and exterior applications. They are commonly used for accent walls, fireplace surrounds, entryways, garages, outdoor kitchens, and exterior facades.\n\nEvan Trevenna\n\nSenior Project Coordinator\n\nHow do I estimate how much GenStone I need for my project?\n\nYou can use the GenStone material calculator or contact a Project Coordinator for a full estimate. Most homeowners measure the square footage of the wall area and then account for corners, trim, and a small 5% waste factor.\n\nTravis Choate\n\nProject Coordinator\n\nDo GenStone panels require maintenance?\n\nGenStone requires very little maintenance. Most installations only need occasional cleaning with mild soap and water to remove dust or debris.\n\nJagger Gottschalk\n\nProject Coordinator\n\nTrending Upgrade Areas this Month\n\nAccent Walls\n\nView Projects\n\nPorch Projects\n\nView Projects\n\nFoundation Cover-Up\n\nView Projects",
